I’m building the verdicts from deterministic text rules plus spot checks, because the lane is 451 records and every object still needs its own deciding quote. The main care point is separating “eligible GLP-1/placebo RCT but no MACE” from active-comparator trials, post hoc analyses, and accounted-trial duplicates.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -NoProfile -Command "@'
import json
snap=json.load(open('cache/glp1-ra-mace-t2d/snapshots/2026-09-15r2-search_v2/records.json',encoding='utf-8'))
prev=json.load(open('C:/meta-harness/outputs/search_v2/verification/glp1-ra-mace-t2d/glp1-ra-mace-t2d.json',encoding='utf-8'))
caps=[x['id'] for x in prev if x.get('verdict')=='NOT_VERIFIED_CAP']
recs={r['id']:r for r in snap['records']}
for i in caps:
    r=recs[i]
    if r.get('id_type')"'!='"'pmid':
        continue
    pubs=';'.join(r.get('pubtypes') or [])
    print(f\"{i}\\t{r.get('year','')}\\t{r.get('nct','')}\\t{pubs}\\t{r.get('title','')}\")
